I left out the enrichment fetch. This node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0`, so it has no HTTP authority. Importing `http-client` would go beyond what the graph allows, and the host would refuse the call anyway. `run-info` also has no text field to use as `q`. If you want enrichment, the graph needs to give some node an `HTTPClient` handle whose allowlist includes `metadata.internal.example`.

The earlier failure came from my made-up fallback feed URL, which is outside the allowlist. This version removes it and returns only what is in the store. It also parses newline-, comma- and JSON-array-style values, and checks both the `urls` and `subscriptions` keys.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{run-info, subscription-list};

    import aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(info: run-info) -> subscription-list;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_read;

struct Node;

fn parse_urls(raw: &str) -> Vec<String> {
    raw.split(|c: char| c == '\n' || c == '\r' || c == ',' || c == '\u{1e}')
        .map(|s| {
            s.trim()
                .trim_matches(|c: char| c == '[' || c == ']' || c.is_whitespace())
                .trim_matches('"')
                .trim()
        })
        .filter(|s| !s.is_empty() && !s.starts_with('#'))
        .map(str::to_owned)
        .collect()
}

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(_info: RunInfo) -> SubscriptionList {
        // Read the subscription list from the one store this node may read.
        // No URLs are invented here: anything the node emits is fetched
        // downstream, and only the configured subscriptions are in scope.
        let mut urls: Vec<String> = Vec::new();
        for key in ["urls", "subscriptions"] {
            if let Some(raw) = state_read::get(key) {
                urls = parse_urls(&raw);
                if !urls.is_empty() {
                    break;
                }
            }
        }

        // Stable order, no duplicates.
        let mut seen: Vec<String> = Vec::with_capacity(urls.len());
        for u in urls {
            if !seen.contains(&u) {
                seen.push(u);
            }
        }

        // ensures present(urls): the field is always populated.
        SubscriptionList { urls: seen }
    }
}

export!(Node);
